<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10093"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 12:16 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text--><a href="http://www.kansas.com/mld/kansas/news/state/11027898.htm"><b>Lookie where mah name done showed up!!!</b></a> <BR> <BR>Quote from the Wichita Eagle/Kansas.com article linked above: <BR> <BR><i>&#34;...Steve Huff, an operatic tenor from Atlanta who maintains a BTK page on his Web log, or blog, speculated in December that the killer would be a balding, stocky, mustachioed neat freak who wore glasses with heavy frames...</i><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10093-->
<!--Post: 10099--><!--Time: 1109754317-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10099"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ivy_leaguer<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->10-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 1:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, <BR> <BR>Congratulations. I have visited your website a few times during the last week and have been impressed by it. I was surprised to discover you are a tenor. I thought you may be a writer or journalist. Your mastery of the English language led to that conclusion. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10099-->
<!--Post: 10102--><!--Time: 1109756783-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10102"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 1:46 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->From <u>you</u>, my friend, this is <b>high praise</b>, and I am grateful.  <BR> <BR>My first love is the word, and through a rather convoluted series of events in my life, that love for language led to singing. I&#39;m a lirico-spinto tenor if defined by the Italian school - a lyric voice with dramatic power. I&#39;m about to make my debut with a small opera company one state over in a leading role - two, actually - Turiddu in <i>Cavalleria Rusticana</i> and Canio in <i>I Pagliacci</i>. I just made my &#34;second&#34; professional debut with the Atlanta Opera in a small role in <i>La Boheme</i>. <i>&#40;I made my first professional debut in 1994 and then, for a multitude of reasons, went into semi-retirement, singing-wise. That&#39;s over.&#41;</i> It&#39;s a truly bizarre profession for a redheaded redneck from South Nashville, but I work with it. I just drink Budweiser at Opera Board Galas instead of a fine merlot, or a &#34;nice chianti&#34;. <BR> <BR>Tell you the truth, if somebody wanted to pay me to write about this, though, I&#39;d do it. Writing is a passion all it&#39;s own, I guess. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10102-->
<!--Post: 10139--><!--Time: 1109782592-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10139"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 8:56 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, <BR> <BR>Just caught you on the AP wire! <BR> <BR>Nixon in China, Harvey Milk, The Death of Klinghoffer. Do you see where I’m headed with this? <BR> <BR>Yes, straight into the land of poor taste, but can you say Sweeny Todd? <BR> <BR>Love your posts, love your blogs, love the opera. <BR> <BR>LostDog <BR>President Steve Huff Fan Club <BR>Opera Pacific season ticket holder <BR>Funky Drummer/Latin Percussionista/ Groovemaker <BR>Currently raising a 5th grade honor band trumpeter and 2013 Thelonius Monk Institute Finalist  <BR> <BR> <BR>Hey Prisoner #27876593, <BR> <BR>Look who’s in the newspaper now. <BR> <BR> <BR>PS OperaMan, <BR> <BR>Stick with the Bud, there&#39;s no such thing as a fine merlot! Do they serve Train Wrecks at those galas? <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10139-->
<!--Post: 10143--><!--Time: 1109784856-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10143"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 9:34 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Thanks, Lost - <BR> <BR>I wasn&#39;t sure how to take you at first, I can admit that, but I appreciate you greatly now. You&#39;re damn funny, you know that, don&#39;t you? <BR> <BR>And Sweeney Todd? Well - it&#39;s probably because of the Demon Barber of Fleet Street that I sing opera today - I had that musical memorized by the time I was 12. I am being quite literal - I bought the original broadway cast album, with Angela Lansbury <i>&#40;there is no other Missus Lovett, sorry, Patti Lupone&#41;</i>, and Len Cariou as Todd - whom George Hearn far outclasses - and had it memorized by the end of the summer.  <BR> <BR><i>&#34;Swing Your Razor wide, Sweeney, <BR>Hold it to the skies, <BR>Freely flows  <BR>the blood of those <BR>Who <b>moralize</b>...&#34;</i> <BR> <BR>Those lyrics are somewhat appropriate to registered republican and devout Lutheran Dennis Rader, you ask me. <BR> <BR>My favorite role I&#39;ve played so far, BTW, is the evil ghost of Peter Quint in Benjamin Britten&#39;s operatic rendering of Henry James&#39;s <i>&#34;Turn of the Screw.&#34;</i> Playing a character like Quint may explain how I could even conceive of getting inside a killer&#39;s head. <BR> <BR>Even though I have Todd memorized, I&#39;ve never actually done the show.  <BR> <BR>Next board gala I attend, I&#39;m heading straight for the cash bar and hunting down the barkeep who knows how to make a Train Wreck - in honor of ole Lost Dog. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 10143-->
<!--Post: 10154--><!--Time: 1109786750-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10154"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Nancydrew<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Nancydrew<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->1-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 10:05 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Off topic &#40;if there is one&#41;.... <BR>Have a performing arts degree myself, and am an Atl girl, and Sweeney Todd was an early favorite.  <BR>&#34;He shaved the faces of gentlemen <BR>Who never thereafter were heard from again....&#34; <BR>Just saying hello.  Congrats on the free press. <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
