<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10183"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Lostdog<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Lostdog<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->2-2005<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, March 02, 2005 - 1:37 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Steve, <BR> <BR>This thread IS all about you babe. <BR> <BR>I wasn&#39;t sure about me at first either! <BR> <BR>Researching this case, I got into a really dark space -- first tme I ever posted anywhere. Check out my last post to BTK &#40;Feb 26&#41;. Clairvoient wrote that &#40;her version of the BTK story&#41;the first week of February, just after she got booted off CBTK! <BR> <BR>I just couldn&#39;t bring myself to post anywhere else. This site had mojo and order. <BR> <BR>&#42;Yes Tom, she was an annoying know-it-all... wait...just like Denny! <BR> <BR>As Clairevoient I was only speaking to BTK -- trying my darnest to get into his head. I dressed up as a woman &#40;again, strangely aroused&#41; because I believed criticisms and spookiness from a female would rattle his cage some... maybe get him to communicate. <BR> <BR>I still think you&#39;re a stud, but in a purely heterosexual man-love kind of way. My wife thinks I&#39;m about 13% gay. You know, likes to cook, decorate, thrilled with the art direction in the film version of West Side Story... never watched a whole football game all the way through...Sex with a man? I don&#39;t know how you gals out there do it.. they&#39;re so hairy and smelly... <BR> <BR>Wow suddenly it&#39;s all about ME! Sorry, that happens a lot.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
