<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST10247"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Steve_huff<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Steve_huff<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, March 03, 2005 - 12:40 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Audrey, that makes two of us. After the initial kind of awed feeling I had on seeing the guy I had an insecurity bout and went back and double-checked everything I&#39;d written...then I saw how close I really was - though it should be said that knowing what he must look like and catching him are two vastly different things - and it just creeped me out.  <BR> <BR>Steve Brisendine, the AP reporter who interviewed me, asked me the following before he told me how impressed he&#39;d been by my figuring out BTK&#39;s possible appearance - &#34;Have you ever <i>been</i> to Wichita?&#34; - and I haven&#39;t. So somehow that made my accuracy on his appearance and a couple of key personal traits all the creepier. <BR> <BR>The funniest thing that&#39;s happened was tonight at church I told the choir about the article - after the congratulations my director said, &#39;I can see why you figured that out - you kind of look like him...&#39; <BR> <BR>Erg - I don&#39;t, OKAY? I&#39;m 6&#39;0&#34; with thinning <b>red</b> hair and a redder beard - I wear fashionable frames that are just the right size on my face and am NOT neat. Well-groomed, but NOT neat.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
